<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea intervenes four times - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea intervenes four times - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea intervened in the interbank market at least four times in early morning trading on Monday to limit the won's decline against the dollar, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank denied intervening, as it does routinely.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the won bounced back up to the 844 level after the bank's dollar selling.</p>
<p>The won opened at a six year low of 845.50 and sank further before the central bank stepped in the first time.</p>
<p>The market has been short on dollars due to large import settlements and poor sentiment towards the local unit, traders said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
